---
// Site footer: copyright + license. Static content with no browser events, so
// it stays a plain .astro component — in Astro that means it ships literally
// zero JavaScript (the same reasoning as the Next server component, just with a
// stronger guarantee). Rendered *outside* <main> in src/pages/index.astro so it
// spans the full width and isn't swept into the main content landmark.
//
// No data-avatar-react on the license link (unlike SocialLinks): the avatar
// lives in a sticky lane *inside* <main>, which has scrolled out of view by the
// time you reach the footer — a hover reaction here would never be seen.

// Evaluated at build time (the site is statically generated), so this is baked
// into the HTML and refreshes on every deploy. Computing it in a client island
// instead would risk a mismatch at the turn of the year and ship needless JS.
const year = new Date().getFullYear();
---

{/* Its own max-w-7xl + mx-auto so it lines up with <main> even though it sits
    outside it. Tokens (text-muted, foreground/10) keep it theme-aware. */}
<footer
  class="mx-auto max-w-7xl border-t border-foreground/10 px-6 py-8 text-center text-sm text-muted"
>
  <p>© {year} Kaushal Patel</p>
  {/* Astro strips whitespace that is only a newline + indentation between text
      and an adjacent tag, so the spaces around the link have to be explicit.
      `{' '}` (the same idiom JSX needs) is the tidiest way to say "a space
      belongs here" without collapsing the markup onto one long line. */}
  <p class="mt-1">
    Code licensed under{' '}
    <a
      href="https://github.com/krazykaushal/krazyk-portfolio/blob/main/LICENSE"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
      class="underline underline-offset-2 transition-colors hover:text-foreground"
    >
      MIT
    </a>{' '}
    &middot; Content &amp; artwork all rights reserved
  </p>
</footer>
